From: Project Luma <luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: Power down UFS during system suspend on Milos

Backport of mainline fb2a238f15f0.

On Milos the UFS PHY GDSC is turned off on every system suspend and the PHY
loses its register state, so exiting hibern8 on resume fails and the error
handler resets the host:

  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: ufshcd_uic_hibern8_exit: hibern8 exit failed. ret = 5
  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: __ufshcd_wl_resume: hibern8 exit failed 5

Set no_phy_retention so system suspend uses UFS_PM_LVL_5 (device powered
down, link off) and the link is brought up again on resume.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2982,6 +2982,10 @@ static void ufs_qcom_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		platform_device_msi_free_irqs_all(hba->dev);
 }
 
+static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_milos_drvdata = {
+	.no_phy_retention = true,
+};
+
 static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata = {
 	.quirks = UFSHCD_QUIRK_BROKEN_LSDBS_CAP,
 	.no_phy_retention = true,
@@ -2993,6 +2997,7 @@ static const struct ufs_qcom_drvdata ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata = {
 
 static const struct of_device_id ufs_qcom_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,milos-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_milos_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
